**About Us** 




 AGAP2 is a European engineering and IT consulting group, part of the MoOngy Group, with over 10,000 employees and a presence in 14 countries.




 In Italy since 2018, with offices in Milan, Brescia, Parma, La Spezia and Rome, we are experiencing strong growth and expanding our team. We are looking for dynamic, ambitious people who are ready to get involved in an environment that values human relationships, professional growth and technological innovation.










**Role Description** 




 We are looking for a
 **Senior Consultant / Manager Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance** 
 to join an important international ERP rollout project, with a focus on
 **Finance processes, localizations and regulatory requirements for Sweden** 
 .




 The resource will be involved in the implementation, configuration, localization and functional support activities of
 **Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance** 
 , working closely with the global project team and local business users.




 The ideal candidate combines solid hands-on knowledge of the application with proven implementation experience, a strong understanding of financial and accounting processes, and expertise in country-specific localizations. The role requires the ability to translate local business and regulatory requirements into functional designs and system configurations aligned with the Global Core Model.




 Strong skills in requirements analysis, gap analysis, functional documentation, testing support, user training and assistance during Go-Live and Post Go-Live phases are essential.




**Fluent written and spoken English is mandatory** 
 , as the role involves conducting workshops, supporting business users and communicating with international stakeholders.




 The role involves a
 **full-time engagement in a fully remote working arrangement** 
 .










**Your Role** 



* Lead and support requirements-gathering workshops with local Key Users and Finance stakeholders, conducting activities in English and documenting business and regulatory requirements;
* Analyze gaps between the Global Core Model and the specific needs of Sweden, Denmark and the UK, identifying localizations, deviations and change requests;
* Support the functional design, implementation and configuration of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance;
* Work on the main modules in scope, including Accounts Receivable, Accounts Payable, General Ledger, Budgeting, Fixed Assets and Cash and Bank Management;
* Configure financial and accounting processes to address country-specific requirements, working with local Finance and tax stakeholders to validate the proposed solutions;
* Support the implementation and validation of localizations covering tax processes, statutory reporting, invoicing, banking and payment requirements;
* Draft and review Functional Design Documents related to local integrations, reports, output documents and technical customizations;
* Collaborate with technical teams as the functional point of reference to ensure the correct translation of business and regulatory requirements into application solutions;
* Coordinate with local stakeholders to validate financial reports, output documents and localization settings against local requirements;
* Support the preparation and localization of test scenarios and test scripts in English, including scenarios addressing country-specific Finance requirements;
* Participate in SIT and UAT activities, supporting defect analysis, issue prioritization and resolution of functional problems;
* Guide and support local Key Users during the User Acceptance Testing phase, providing functional clarifications and coordination with the project team;
* Support data migration validation activities, verifying master data, open balances, completeness, accuracy and consistency with local requirements;
* Plan, prepare and coordinate remote training and enablement activities for end-users, preparing training materials and support sessions;
* Provide remote support during Go-Live and Post Go-Live phases, with a particular focus on daily financial operations, period-end and month-end closing;
* Monitor the progress of local activities, reporting milestones, risks, issues and corrective actions;
* Act as a functional point of contact for local Finance users, ensuring clear communication with the global team in English;
* Collaborate with Project Managers, stakeholders, technical teams and functional streams, participating in regular meetings and providing structured status updates.









**Requirements** 



* Previous experience as a Senior Consultant, Functional Consultant, Solution Consultant or Manager on Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance / Finance & Operations projects;
* Solid hands-on experience in the implementation, configuration and rollout of D365 Finance, including localization and Post Go-Live support;
* Strong functional knowledge of Finance modules, particularly Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, General Ledger, Fixed Assets, Budgeting and Cash and Bank Management;
* A strong understanding of financial and accounting processes, including their configuration and integration within the ERP;
* Proven experience with country-specific localizations and the implementation of local accounting, tax and regulatory requirements relevant to
 **Sweden, Denmark and/or the United Kingdom** 
 ;
* Ability to translate local requirements into functional specifications and system configurations, coordinating validation with local Finance and tax stakeholders;
* Experience in requirements gathering, conducting workshops with business users and drafting functional documentation;
* Ability to perform gap analysis against a Global Core Model, identifying localizations, deviations and change requests;
* Experience in drafting Functional Design Documents for integrations, reports, output documents and customizations;
* Knowledge of ERP testing processes, including SIT, UAT, defect management and end-user support;
* Experience in data migration validation, user training, Go-Live and Post Go-Live support activities;
* Knowledge of or exposure to integrations related to customer invoicing, financial reporting, credit management, bank statement imports, payment file generation and payroll GL journals;
* **Fluent written and spoken English** 
 , with the ability to independently lead workshops, produce functional documentation and communicate effectively with international stakeholders;
* Ability to work effectively in a fully remote environment, coordinating activities with distributed project teams and local business users;
* Excellent communication, analytical, problem-solving and stakeholder management skills;
* Ability to work in international, structured environments focused on meeting project milestones.









**What We Offer** 



* The gross annual salary for this role ranges from
 **EUR 90,000 to EUR 110,000** 
 .



 The position is framed within the
 **Italian National Collective Bargaining Agreement for the Commerce and Tertiary Sector** 
 applied by our company. The positioning within the range will be defined based on technical skills, specific experience in the role and the outcome of the selection process, according to objective and predefined criteria. In the case of profiles with exceptional characteristics compared to the indicated range, a review may be considered subject to internal approval.



* **Fully remote working arrangement** 
 ;
* Participation in an international ERP rollout focused on Finance processes and country-specific localizations;
* Operational support and constant interaction with functional, technical and project management teams;
* A dynamic, collaborative environment focused on professional growth;
* Development opportunities within a fast-growing international group.









**The world needs you** 




 AGAP2 is an equal opportunities employer: we believe that all forms of diversity are a source of mutual enrichment. We are committed to ensuring an inclusive work environment in which every individual can bring unique value to our organization. Therefore, we welcome applications regardless of age, gender, nationality, disability, sexual orientation, religion or marital status.




 Furthermore, we remain committed to supporting candidates belonging to protected categories pursuant to Articles 1 and 18 of Italian Law 68/99.




 Personal data will be processed in accordance with the provisions of EU Regulation 2016/679.79.
